{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Identity arrives here\nThe Bearer Token Extractor lifts the caller's access token off the Authorization header into the execution context. A key icon on the Webhook node confirms it is active.\n\nWebhook is the only trigger this extractor supports. Chat and MCP triggers seal the identity instead, which is affected by a known OAuth refresh bug.",
        "height": 272,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "23cd40fb-d452-461e-9df0-ad229084ca44",
      "name": "Sticky Note Identity",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        656,
        384
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Runs as the caller, not as you\nThe Gmail credential needs \"Set up for end-user credentials\" enabled, and this workflow must name your resolver under Settings > Dynamic credential resolver.\n\nn8n maps the caller's subject claim to that person's own stored Google token. There is no fallback to the credential's own account: an unresolved credential fails the node and takes the error branch.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "e57a1778-1b0b-4b8c-8859-c1797acf34e8",
      "name": "Sticky Note Credential",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        656,
        1056
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "end-user-gmail",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "52da8b3a-4e04-4bba-96b0-1206f4a309c0",
      "name": "Receive Call From App",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        656,
        784
      ],
      "webhookId": "5e6890ce-5333-4789-99e2-2c0cfe621e90"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "getAll",
        "limit": 3,
        "filters": {
          "readStatus": "both"
        }
      },
      "id": "9d668e19-ef89-46b0-8800-2ff888c34e0b",
      "name": "Fetch Callers Recent Emails",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        784
      ],
      "webhookId": "d8441559-c918-48d3-8304-617276f1a3b4",
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "from",
              "name": "from",
              "value": "={{ $json.From }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "subject",
              "name": "subject",
              "value": "={{ $json.Subject }}",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "ccbfa0de-5b55-45f1-9eb2-8221e67a72fa",
      "name": "Keep From And Subject",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        1104,
        688
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://gmail.googleapis.com/gmail/v1/users/me/profile",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "gmailOAuth2",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "d923c29f-a0b6-4d61-815b-cab0a14c2aee",
      "name": "Get Connected Account",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [
        1328,
        688
      ],
      "executeOnce": true,
      "notes": "Gmail asks for no identity scope, so the stored token carries no email claim. users.getProfile is the only way to learn which account this run authenticated as."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "={{ { account: $('Get Connected Account').first().json.emailAddress, messages: $('Keep From And Subject').all().map(item => item.json) } }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "470097e1-8a64-447e-9c72-a913ca405736",
      "name": "Return Emails To App",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.5,
      "position": [
        1552,
        688
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "json",
        "responseBody": "{\"error\":\"gmail_not_connected\",\"message\":\"No Gmail token is stored for this caller. Call the execution-status endpoint and follow the authorizationUrl to connect.\"}",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 424
